  "claims": [
    "Directed plans admit executable structural equality via an untyped shape decoder. Decoding their encoding returns the original typed plan; equal shapes imply equal indexed plans.",
    "Every Cell constructor has a finite-arity inference rule. Judgments include both typed boundary plans AND the exact whole-diagram declared condition support. No new higher root is introduced.",
    "Structural interning compares actual rule payloads and parent indices, not rendered strings. A separate unshared producer is also checked by the same checker.",
    "A successful compilation returns a Verified certificate with its actual checker acceptance proof at the original boundary and support. Soundness is independent of producer correctness.",
    "Accepted shared data has a geometric interpretation with exactly the recorded support, a probabilistic comparison under that finite support, and a computational certified-reduction comparison under a checked corresponding model.",
    "Finite-support cached-condition repair reconstructs the probabilistic comparison in the checked updated model.",
    "The same typed certificate also has an ordinary conditional-kernel/loss-equality interpretation when the model conditions are supplied globally; this baseline does not retain source Cell syntax in its carrier.",
    "Actual MAC terminalCoherence outputs for stages 0 through 4 are compiled and accepted, with boundary-plan and condition metadata included. The previous artificial repeated-comparison family is not substituted."
  ],
